Here is the full **testsmells.org 19-smell academic audit** for your integration test suite.

---

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1.0 · .NET 10  
**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`  
**Integration marker:** `[TestCategory("Integration")]` — calibration rules applied throughout.

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

## Findings by Severity

### ❶ Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — HIGH

**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)  
**Why it matters:** This test inserts 100 rows but never asserts anything. MSTest marks it as "passed" even if every `Insert` silently corrupts data or is a no-op. It provides false confidence.

```csharp
// CURRENT — no assertion
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
```

**Fix — verify the side-effect:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** The test is a no-op gatekeeper — bugs pass through undetected.

---

### ❷ Sleepy Test — HIGH

**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)  
**Why it matters:** `Thread.Sleep(3000)` adds 3 seconds of dead wall-clock time. If the notification mechanism becomes faster or slower, the test either wastes time or flakes. Even in integration tests this is a smell — the sleep is a blind wait, not a coordinated synchronization.

```csharp
// CURRENT — blind sleep
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix — poll with a timeout:**

```csharp
// Retry with back-off up to a deadline
var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(5);
while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
{
    if (DateTime.UtcNow > deadline)
        Assert.Fail("Notification was not sent within 5 s.");
    await Task.Delay(100);
}
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Non-deterministic failures in CI; cumulative suite slowdown as more sleepy tests are added.

---

### ❸ Conditional Test Logic — HIGH

**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)  
**Why it matters:** The `if/else` means only one branch of assertions ever executes per run. If the production code incorrectly returns a `PremiumUser`, the `DiscountRate` branch runs; if it returns a base `User`, the `Name` branch runs — neither case validates the *expected* type.

```csharp
// CURRENT — conditional assertion paths
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix — assert the expected type explicitly:**

```csharp
// Know what you expect and assert it
var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.IsInstanceOfType<User>(loaded);   // or PremiumUser if that's expected
Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
```

If both types are valid scenarios, split into two test methods — one that sets up a premium user and asserts `PremiumUser`, another for a regular user.

**Risk if unfixed:** Hidden testing gap — the untested branch could silently harbour a bug.

---

### ❹ Assertion Roulette — MEDIUM

**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)  
**Why it matters:** Four consecutive assertions with no message parameters. When one fails, MSTest reports `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>.` — but you must read the source to know which property was being checked. In a CI log with 200 tests, this slows triage.

```csharp
// CURRENT — 4 assertions, zero messages
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix — add diagnostic messages:**

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should match inserted value");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should match inserted value");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slow failure diagnosis, especially in CI pipelines.

---

## Smells Scanned & Found Clean (15 / 19)

| Smell | Verdict | Notes |
|-------|---------|-------|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean | In-memory SQLite — hermetic, no external files/network/env-vars |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean | Max 3 distinct production methods per test; appropriate for integration scope |
| Magic Number Test | ✅ Clean | `3` after adding 3 items, `10` after adding 10 — contextually obvious |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean | No `.ToString()` comparisons |
| Exception Handling | ✅ Clean | No `try`/`catch` blocks |
| General Fixture | ✅ Clean | `_connection` and `_repository` are used by all 8 tests |
| Ignored / Disabled Test | ✅ Clean | No `[Ignore]` or `Skip` attributes |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean | No duplicated assertion statements |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Clean | Multiple tests call `Insert`/`GetByEmail` but each tests distinct behavior |
| Constructor Initialization | ✅ Clean | Properly uses `[TestInitialize]` |
| Default Test | ✅ Clean | Class is meaningfully named |
| Redundant Print | ✅ Clean | No `Console.WriteLine` or debug output |
| Redundant Assertion | ✅ Clean | No tautological assertions |
| Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean | In-memory database, no assumed external resources |
| Empty Test | ✅ Clean | No empty method bodies |

---

## Smell-Free Patterns Worth Highlighting

- **`DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`** — textbook Arrange-Act-Assert with a single clear assertion (`Assert.IsNull`). Excellent.
- **`ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`** — contextually self-documenting count assertion plus `CollectionAssert`. Clean and readable.
- **`InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity`** — properly uses `async/await` with `Task.WhenAll` and validates outcome. Well-structured concurrency test.

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | **Assertion-Free Test** (`BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors`) | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count)` | ~2 min |
| 2 | **Conditional Test Logic** (`GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType`) | Assert expected type explicitly; split if both types are valid | ~10 min |
| 3 | **Sleepy Test** (`NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay`) | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with polling/retry loop | ~15 min |
| 4 | **Assertion Roulette** (`InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase`) | Add message parameter to each assertion | ~3 min |

Fix items 1–2 first — they can mask real bugs today. Item 3 prevents flakiness and speeds up CI. Item 4 is a quality-of-life improvement for failure diagnosis.
